@page "/"

<PageTitle>Civic Permits</PageTitle>

<h1>Civic Permits</h1>

<p class="lead">
    Apply for a building, sign, event or vendor permit, and follow your application, online.
</p>

<ul class="cards">
    <li>
        <h2>Find the right permit</h2>
        <p>See every kind of permit the office offers, what it costs and how long it takes.</p>
        <p><a href="/permits">Browse permits</a></p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <h2>Check a permit</h2>
        <p>Have a permit number? See whether it has been issued and when it expires. No account needed.</p>
        <p><a href="/lookup">Check a permit</a></p>
    </li>
    <AuthorizeView>
        <Authorized>
            <li>
                <h2>Your work</h2>
                <p>Continue where you left off.</p>
                <p><a href="/applications">Go to @(context.User.IsInRole("Applicant") ? "my applications" : context.User.IsInRole("Inspector") ? "my inspections" : "the applications")</a></p>
            </li>
        </Authorized>
        <NotAuthorized>
            <li>
                <h2>Apply for a permit</h2>
                <p>Make an account, then apply in three short steps. You can save a draft and come back to it.</p>
                <p><a href="/account/register">Make an account</a> or <a href="/account/login">sign in</a></p>
            </li>
        </NotAuthorized>
    </AuthorizeView>
</ul>

<h2>How it works</h2>
<ol>
    <li>Choose the permit you need.</li>
    <li>Describe the project and where it will happen.</li>
    <li>Check your answers and send the application.</li>
    <li>A clerk reviews it. They may ask you to change something, and they always say why.</li>
    <li>Once approved, pay the fee at the counter. If an inspection is needed, an inspector visits. Then the permit is issued.</li>
</ol>

<p>
    This site works without JavaScript and is built and tested against WCAG 2.1 AA. If something does not work for you,
    that is a defect; please tell the permit office.
</p>
